{
  "program": "L2",
  "title": "Adjacent word edges remain associated under exact-length shuffles inside each line on public pages",
  "statement": "On the fixed public practice partitions, adjacent word edges retain association after conditioning on the exact EVA-basic lengths of both words and permuting intact certain words only within the same line and length. On 34 evaluation pages the conditional MI is 0.533009 bits over 4796 pairs in ZL (null mean 0.445336; excess 0.087673) and 0.512346 over 4740 pairs in IT (null mean 0.420688; excess 0.091658). All199 shuffled values are below the observation in each edition, so the plus-one one-sided p is0.005. Training partitions also return p0.005, with excess0.122019 and0.117486. The hypothesis, exact-length rule,199 replicates, seed and p<=0.01 decision were saved before the analysis run. The null preserves each line word multiset, literal uncertainty barriers and the word-length sequence; this tests more than ordinary word-order shuffling. The independent entropy decomposition matches the direct CMI to1.3e-15. This is a diagnostic of residual statistical association, not evidence of semantics: position-specific glyph distributions, spelling conventions, transcription and production procedures remain possible explanations. Raw plug-in CMI is biased; only the comparison with identical length strata and sample layout is interpreted. No hidden result is requested or inferred, and prior edge-MI facts are not resubmitted.",
  "check": "Add a reviewed trusted DSL statistic for edge conditional mutual information given exact left/right EVA-basic lengths, with a null permuting intact certain words inside (original line, exact glyph length) cells. Preserve missing or uncertain tokens as literal barriers. Require >=30 adjacent and potentially movable pairs; refuse a constant null. Test the CMI with an independent entropy decomposition and invariants for line inventory and length sequence. After human review and merge, preregister one new fact with p<=0.01,199 permutations in both ZL and independent IT. No magnitude threshold chosen from this pilot. Test whether existing public meaningless generators reproduce it before interpreting it as evidence of language.",
  "on_path": false,
  "hard": false,
  "evidence": {
    "plan": {
      "hypothesis": "Adjacent word edges remain associated beyond the exact lengths of both words and the line word inventory.",
      "statistic": "Weighted conditional mutual information of last/first EVA-basic glyph given exact left/right EVA-basic lengths; bits per adjacent pair.",
      "selection": "Certain literal adjacent words of P lines only. Uncertain/empty words stay barriers; never join across a line.",
      "null": "Permute intact certain words only within (original line, exact EVA-basic length) cells; all positions and uncertain barriers fixed.",
